{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/839563-totem-bonuses-and-caps","id":839563,"title":"Totem bonuses and caps.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-29T17:44:45-08:00","id":839563,"title":"Totem bonuses and caps.","content":"Do totem bonuses granted to things like skills allow the player to exceed the usual cap of 5? Some say they can. Others make no mention of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1546-great-cthulhu","name":"Great Cthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1546_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T18:01:46-08:00","id":839577,"title":"","content":"I would say they can, after all it's totem power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T21:25:56-08:00","id":839673,"title":"","content":"That's always been tough for me because some totems (like Black Tortoise, Turtle, Fenris) actually go out of their way to state &quot;even if this brings the character over 5&quot;, while most do not. So I always wondered if it only happened for these characters like it was a special feature for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T00:05:44-08:00","id":839726,"title":"","content":"It might make a difference, whether each pack member gets the bonus, or if it is in form of dice, to be assigned as a bonus. Generally I grant the bonuses beyond the cap of 5 - for my impression is, that most authors, editors didn't bother make their wording clear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T00:16:11-08:00","id":839731,"title":"","content":"Back in Revised, there was some comment that the original intent was that unless it says it raises things above 5, it doesn't.<br /> <br /> Of course, that's kind of silly. 6+ traits aren't actually that strong, and the Totems are a complete mess of both lack of clarity and any concept of &quot;balance.&quot; I'll never really understand why WtA insists on pages and pages of Totems, most of which never get used, instead of fraction of the page count just making a decent Totem creation rule-set. Forsaken's managed to get a functional one out in its 1e, and a decent one out in its 2e. Apocalypse is on W20 and still hasn't bothered.<br /> <br /> Sorry... ranting a bit I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T00:19:15-08:00","id":839733,"title":"","content":"No problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T01:01:53-08:00","id":839741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/839563-totem-bonuses-and-caps?p=839731#post839731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry... ranting a bit I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries. That's what we come for <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T01:12:57-08:00","id":839744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/839563-totem-bonuses-and-caps?p=839741#post839741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No worries. That's what we stay for <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>FIFY...........","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T01:50:18-08:00","id":839749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/839563-totem-bonuses-and-caps?p=839744#post839744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> FTFY...........</div> </div> </div> </div>Fixed <b>T</b>hat For You. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T03:38:52-08:00","id":839779,"title":"","content":"<i>Ponders ranting about his rants are usually under-appreciated by you guys.<br /> <br /> Gets distracted by wanting to rant about hating &quot;Fixed that for you.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> So, anyway. Anyone else familiar with the Forsaken 2e Totem creation rules seeing any particular problems with converting it to WtA? The bonus for fulfilling the Totem's Aspiration would need to change (either regain Rage/Gnosis/WP as appropriate to Totem type, or temporary Renown, or end of story XP bonus all work). The Totem Ponts to XP granted to spend on pack traits chart would need to change (x5 should do it). You can keep the WtA version of building the Totem's stats the WtA way since that stay's largely the same just with different spreads for the different ways spirits are modeled.<br /> <br /> The only thing I can think of that would be a problem is how Forsaken 2e handles Bans due to the differences in how the two games handle spirit ranks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T04:55:20-08:00","id":839801,"title":"","content":"Sadly, no I'm clueless about their totems. I pretty much skipped on the mechanics after the fluff left me meh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T15:24:02-08:00","id":840203,"title":"","content":"The base mechanics are pretty simple really:<br /> <br /> 1) All Totems have an Aspiration. This is a long term goal the spirit has that the pack works towards. It could be a discrete task that's too broad in scope to really finish but the pack can make progress towards (example suitable to WtA: resurrecting one of the lost Breeds), or something more simple that would be never ending (ex: protecting the natural habitat of the spirit's physical kin). Every time the pack does something significant towards this, they get a bonus. In 2e WtF it's a Beat, which is ~1 XP in WoD value. But as I mentioned above other rewards could work for WtA.<br /> <br /> 2) All Totems have a Ban. This is something the spirit can't do, and the pack doesn't do as part of their bond to the Totem. This is pretty much like the existing Bans in WtA, though strictly prohibition based. 2e WtF has a stronger mechanical cost for failing to follow your Totem's Ban. The first time a character fails to uphold it, they get it mystically forced on them more directly until they make up to the spirit, and the second time they lose all their Totem dots as well which they'll have to buy back rather strenuously to get back in the Totem's good graces.<br /> <br /> The biggest sticking point in converting this, is that WtF Bans scale with the power of the spirit, so as more Totem dots go into the spirit, its Rank will increase, and its Ban will get harsher; unlike WtA Totem Bans which are relatively constant. In WtF there are more mechanical spirit Ranks, which have a more set interaction with how powerful the spirit is. WtA has less spirit Ranks, and has a lot more overlap between powerful lower rank vs weak higher rank.<br /> <br /> 3) For every X total dots in Totem, you get Y XP (keeping in mind that 2e WtF XP is flat costs like freebies instead of scaling). The group spends that XP as if buying traits to determine what bonuses the Totem grants. Whatever they buy, all members of the pack gets it. Traits like Attributes and Skills can be increased above normal caps. Things like Merits and Backgrounds that don't really work that way refund you for the overlap and you can spend them else where. So if a Totem gives the pack Acute Senses (Hearing), and PC that started with that would get a different 1 dot Merit instead.<br /> <br /> 4) For every X dots in Totem, the spirit's Attributes and powers increase (you don't have to pick from a chart like WtA, it's automatic when have enough dots invested).<br /> <br /> And... that's it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T23:23:39-08:00","id":844943,"title":"","content":"For whatever it's worth, I compiled a list of all W:tA totems into one place and put it on Google Docs. The link is in my signature. And, as I mention on the doc file, none of the totems have been play-tested for balance; it's just a straight-from-the-books compilation of all the published totems, current as of W20.<br /> <br /> But yeah, a totem generation guide for W;tA would be damn nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T14:43:28-08:00","id":845282,"title":"","content":"so i don't want to open a new discussion, so i ask here...<br /> <br /> How work the Background Totem? and it's possibile create a totem only for the pack?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6052-rettile-blitch","name":"Rettile&Blitch","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T15:13:24-08:00","id":845301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rettile&amp;amp;Blitch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/839563-totem-bonuses-and-caps?p=845282#post845282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so i don't want to open a new discussion, so i ask here...<br /> <br /> How work the Background Totem? and it's possibile create a totem only for the pack?</div> </div> </div> </div>Each dot in the background that the pack mates have go towards paying off the initial cost of the totem, after that the points can buy bonuses for the pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T15:16:34-08:00","id":845306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/839563-totem-bonuses-and-caps?p=845301#post845301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Each dot in the background that the pack mates have go towards paying off the initial cost of the totem, after that the points can buy bonuses for the pack.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> an example?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6052-rettile-blitch","name":"Rettile&Blitch","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T15:20:43-08:00","id":845309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rettile&amp;amp;Blitch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/839563-totem-bonuses-and-caps?p=845306#post845306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> an example?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't have my books in front of me but they allow such things as letting the pack to communicate over any distance, summon an avatar of the totem to fight along side the pack and boosting the stats of said avatar","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T15:21:19-08:00","id":845310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rettile&amp;amp;Blitch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/839563-totem-bonuses-and-caps?p=845306#post845306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> an example?</div> </div> </div> </div>Say the totem costs 5 background points. The pack buys, in total, 15 points. The 5 points pay for the totem cost, while the rest can be used to add powers/skills to the totem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T15:32:41-08:00","id":845322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/839563-totem-bonuses-and-caps?p=845301#post845301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each dot in the background that the pack mates have go towards paying off the initial cost of the totem, after that the points can buy bonuses for the pack.</div> </div> </div> </div>The points in excess of the Totem's base value can also go towards boosting the Totem spirit directly (increasing it's Attributes, adding to its Charms, etc).<br /> <br /> ---------<br /> <br /> An example of how things work with W20 RAW:<br /> <br /> Lets say the pack if following Raven, and we have 5 PCs, all starting with 1 dot in Totem.<br /> <br /> Raven's base cost is 5, and the current pack total is 5, so they get the base Raven bonuses, and a raven-spirit with 8 points to divide between the base spirit Attributes as well as the Reform and Airt Sense Charms.<br /> <br /> A bit down the line the pack has increased their pool to 15 total dots (so 2 more Totem dots per character), leaving them with 10 in excess of the base cost. They can use that to buy a number of boosts.<br /> <br /> The spend 4 points to allow the pack to communicate psychically with each other, 3 points to increase the number of members of the pack that can benefit from Raven's pack bonuses (+3 Survival, +1 Subterfuge, +1 Enigmas) from one to two, 2 points to add the Swift Flight Charm to their raven-spirit, and 1 to let the raven spirit always be able to find them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}